Q=210 misses AP drops: [6, 12]
Q=1260 repairs AP drops: [6, 12, 10, 4, 2, 13, 5, 3, 8, 9, 11, 1, 7]

Radical-blind repair summary
  drop 6: Q=1260 safe reduced denominators [63, 420, 630]; hits whose denom divides 210 = 0
  drop 12: Q=1260 safe reduced denominators [12, 315, 630, 1260]; hits whose denom divides 210 = 0

Interpretation:
  Inside the 1260 divisor lattice, drop 6 uses repeated-prime
  packets with lowest reduced denominator 63=3^2*7.
  Drop 12 uses the dyadic packet 12=2^2*3.
  The radical 210=2*3*5*7 has none of these repeated-prime
  exact-period packets.
  The raw Hill carrier 1260=2^2*3^2*5*7 contains both lanes.
  The crossing quotient 315 sees some 3^2 packets but loses the dyadic lane.

